      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "I really try to be open to that possibility, Doctor. I honestly do. I sit there and tell myself, 'You're just connecting dots that aren't there.' And I want to agree with you, because... well, it would make me a much more reasonable person, wouldn't it? I don't want you to think I'm just ignoring your logic or being difficult. \n\nBut... um... when I actually look at everything from the past year... I know I keep repeating myself, and I'm sorry for that. I know my wife insists it's all just normal office stuff. But the way those late meetings and the little changes in her messages happen... they just line up too precisely to feel accidental. Even when I try my absolute hardest to tell myself it's all in my head, I still feel that private signal in them. It just feels so clearly like it's meant to tell me something she won't say directly. \n\nI'm so sorry, I know that means I'm probably not giving you the answer you're hoping for. Does it make me sound terrible that I just can't seem to let that feeling go, even when you lay it out so clearly for me? I really am trying to be good about this.",
